    "why": "THE LINE BETWEEN A SPLIT AND A GAP, AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS THIS RULE. On the night slot p-ali holds the Friday and nobody holds the Saturday: the weekend is not split between two people, it is short a person, and WHO has to be on duty at all is a coverage template (SL-03, P3) rather than a pairing preference. On the day slot of the same weekend p-ali holds the Friday and p-noor the Saturday, which IS a split and is reported. One world, both answers, so a predicate reporting any weekend whose two days disagree — including against nobody — fails here rather than looking like a stricter reading of the same rule.",
